```
Reason:
When the preparation of a command fails, the failed request is added to the `requeue_list` without updating the original request list (`rqlist`). This results in subsequent requests becoming orphaned, as they are no longer tracked in the original list, leading to attempts to submit an unprepared command.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
rq_list_move(rqlist, &requeue_list, req, prev);
req = prev;
```
